# Performance (RAOS Ch.19)

Full doc: `docs/raos/chapter-19-performance-scalability.md`.

## Goals (targets)

- Home interactive < 2s; home recommendations < 3s.
- Explore category switch (cached) < 1s.
- AI first token < 3s; full reply < 10s (complexity-dependent).
- Itinerary build < 8s; place detail (cached) < 1s.

## Practices

- Multi-level cache: Memory → Disk → Cloud → API.
- Deduplicate concurrent identical place/API requests.
- Preload hot paths; lazy-load reviews/heavy images/insights.
- Parallelize independent fetches before Decision.
- Offline-first for Trip/Place/images/Memory/Workspace where possible.
- Images: thumbnail → medium → original.
- Quota monitors; degrade non-essential requests near limits.
- Smart refresh: update only changed slices.
- Background sync must not block UI.
- Failure path: retry → fallback → cache → partial response (never blank).
- Optimize via PSF/cache/queue/background tasks — not prompt stacking or duplicate APIs.
